WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.030
Good morning, Hank; it's Monday. I'm at Bill
and Eileen's house. Bill and Eileen were my

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.370
first bosses, or at least some of my first
bosses at Booklist magazine. Eileen Cooper

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:10.059
is the reason, of course, that I am an author.
She is an author herself of books like Sam

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:15.370
I Am and The Golden Rule. This is the Korean
edition, because Eileen doesn't have an English

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:20.109
edition, but anyway this book is dedicated
to me. I would show you but the dedication

00:00:20.109 --> 00:00:22.009
is in – is in – is in Korean.

00:00:22.009 --> 00:00:24.960
So Hank your video on Friday was amazing and
I still can't get over the fact that nerdfighters

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.669
found Gussie Manlove even though she wasn't
named Gussie Manlove when she died--she was

00:00:28.669 --> 00:00:33.690
named Audrey Brown, and she wasn't named Gussie
Manlove when she was born--she was named Gussie

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.469
Horsey, which is the worst name ever!

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:40.079
Or at least I thought it was the worst name
ever until I started doing research on the

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:41.079
topic.

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:44.670
So today, Hank, I present to you my list of
six unfortunate names from history.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:48.771
Number six: Dick Trickle. Hank, when it comes
to Dicks you have a lot of unfortunate name

00:00:48.771 --> 00:00:52.449
choices like Dick Sweat, the former congressman,
or Dick Army.

00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:56.980
But to my mind the best at being worst is
Dick Trickle, who was a NASCAR driver. Aside

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:00.580
from being famous for being named Dick Trickle,
Dick Trickle was also famous because he was

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:05.950
the only NASCAR driver in history who had
a hole screwed into his helmet so that he

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:10.030
could smoke in the middle of races. He had
his pit crew install a cigarette lighter in

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:13.920
his stock car, and one time after a race with
very few caution flags he said "That race

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.659
went by so fast I only had time for two cigarettes!"

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:23.130
Number five: Ima Hogg. The daughter of Texas
governor "Big Jim Hogg." Ima Hogg was known

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:27.640
as 'The First Lady of Texas', probably because
no one wants to be known as Ima Hogg. She

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:30.830
was a great patron of the arts, she collected
works by Picasso and Matisse, and she was

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:34.960
a philanthropist, and she also has an honorary
degree meaning that technically her name is

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.009
Dr. Ima Hogg.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:41.399
Number four: Harry Baals. Hank, Harry Baals
has been much in the news lately because there

00:01:41.399 --> 00:01:47.130
is a move by the city of Fort Wayne to name
a building after their beloved former mayor,

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:52.270
Harry Baals. His name really was Harry Baals
and he is a very beloved former mayor. Like,

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:57.180
I hear all the time on talk radio in Indiana
people saying "You know those East Coast people,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.219
they can tell us 'You can't name a building
the Harry Baals Government Center!' Well,

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.900
what this town needs is more Harry Baals."

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:07.219
Number three: Shanda Lear, the daughter of
the guy who founded the Learjet corporation.

00:02:07.219 --> 00:02:11.560
Shanda Lear, uh, grew up to become a lead
singer in swing bands.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:18.290
Number two: Hymen Lipman, who was the first
person to ever attach an eraser to a pencil.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:24.470
And number one: Chris P Bacon, a composer
living in Los Angeles who writes music for

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:30.120
movies. Like, he contributed music to such
music as Gnomeo and Juliet, Michael Clayton,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:36.830
I Am Legend... and, Hank, he wrote the entire
original score for the American classic Space

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.750
Chimps. Also just to reiterate, his name is
Chris P Bacon.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:44.151
So Hank it just goes to show you that merely
having a horrible name like Chris P Bacon

00:02:44.151 --> 00:02:50.430
or Gussie Manlove doesn't mean that you can't
go on to great things like writing the score

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:51.950
for the movie Space Chimps.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:55.370
Funny-named individuals, don't lose hope.
Hank, I'll see you on Wednesday.

